>> Dear list,
>>
>> Hi. In the list at the bottom of the message I put some data about
>> plant volumes and weights in 2 maize genotypes (I have several more,
>> but putting only 2 will be enough for the example). By using 'dlply' I
>> fit one linear model relating weight1~volume1 to each genotype, and
>> them extracted the coefficients with 'ldply'.
>>
>> I want to calculate a new variable based on the 'volume2' values by
>> using the coefficients of each fitted model,(e.g. weight2 = Intercept
>> + slope*volume2).
>
> What "volume2"?
>
>>
>> As I am newly in plyr I don't know how to do it, but I guess it is
>> possible. Can someone help me with this?
>
> Perhaps using this a a model of how to step through a dataframe:
>
> apply(ldply(models, coef), 1, function(x) list(Int = x[2], volcoef=x[3]))
>

Thanks David. 'volume2' is the last variable in the right part of the
dataframe.

I've been able to extract the model coefficients by using apply (as you
mention), but still I have no idea about how to use those coefficients
to calculate a new variable (e.g. 'weight2') using 'volume2' as input

(i.e. weight2 = Intercept + slope*volume2).

Thanks for your help,

Alan.
