>
> I've been able to extract the model coefficients by using apply (as
> you mention), but still I have no idea about how to use those
> coefficients to calculate a new variable (e.g. 'weight2') using
> 'volume2' as input (i.e. weight2 = Intercept + slope*volume2).

When you ran the code you got coefficients from two models:
 > str(ldply(models, coef))
'data.frame':	2 obs. of  3 variables:
  $ genotype   : int  1 2
  $ (Intercept): num  3.84 5.31
  $ volume1    : num  0.951 0.935

How do you intend to use "slope", which I do not see calculated with
any R expressions, as applied to a vector of 270 values of "volume2"?
My half-assed guess: Are you trying to use the value of the "volume1"
and '(Intercept)' coefs in that resultant dataframe for calculation of
an estimated weight on the basis of the "genotype" and 'volume2'
values in the original dataframe? So maybe my question should have
been "What slope?"

Perhaps:

mod.rslt <- ldply(models, coef)
allometry$weight2 <- apply(allometry, 1, function(x) {
                  mod.rslt[ x[2],'(Intercept)'] + # choosing the
(Intercept)
                                                 # on basis of
"genotype" in allometry
                  mod.rslt[ x[2],'volume1']*x[7] })  # same for what I
am guessing is
                                                 # meant by "slope".

> Thanks for your help,
>
> Alan.
